            "officialText": "ax3 + bx2 + cx. 5 Complete the square for expressions in the form ax2 + bx + c. Simplify means give the answer in its simplest form, e.g. 2a2 + 3ab – 1 + 5a2 – 9ab + 4 = 7a2 – 6ab + 3. e.g. expand 3x(2x – 4y), (3x + y)(x – 4y). Includes products of more than two brackets, e.g. expand (x – 2)(x + 3)(2x + 1). Factorise means factorise fully, e.g. 9x2 + 15xy = 3x(3x + 5y).",
