            "topicId": "9700-a2-topic-04",
            "sectionCode": "15.2",
            "outcomeNumber": 3,
            "officialText": "describe the role of gibberellin in the germination of barley (see 16.3.4) 16 Inheritance Genetic information is transmitted from generation to generation to maintain the continuity of life. In sexual reproduction, meiosis introduces genetic variation so that offspring resemble their parents but are not identical to them. Genetic crosses reveal how some features are inherited. The phenotype of organisms is determined partly by the genes that they have inherited and partly by the effect of the environment. Genes determine how organisms develop; gene control in bacteria gives us a glimpse of this process in action.",
