            "topicId": "9700-a2-topic-06",
            "sectionCode": "17.2",
            "outcomeNumber": 1,
            "officialText": "explain that natural selection occurs because populations have the capacity to produce many offspring that compete for resources; in the ‘struggle for existence’, individuals that are best adapted are most likely to survive to reproduce and pass on their alleles to the next generation",
