            "topicId": "9700-a2-topic-06",
            "sectionCode": "17.3",
            "outcomeNumber": 5,
            "officialText": "ecological and behavioural separation (sympatric speciation) 18 Classification, biodiversity and conservation Classification systems attempt to order all the organisms that exist on Earth according to their characteristics and evolutionary relationships with one another. There are opportunities in this topic for candidates to observe different species in their locality and assess species distribution and abundance. Fieldwork is an important part of a biological education because it provides opportunities to appreciate and analyse biodiversity, and to study the interactions between organisms and their environment. The biodiversity of",
