            "officialText": "outline the role in conservation of the International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) and the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES) 19 Genetic technology The discovery in the early 1950s of the structure of DNA by Watson and Crick, supported by the work of Franklin, Wilkins and Chargaff, and discoveries since, have led to many applications of genetic technology in areas of medicine, agriculture and forensic science. This topic relies heavily on prior knowledge of DNA and",
